This game is a perfect example of a game that hasn't aged all that well, and come to think of it, how come people enjoyed it before and now, and worst yet, nominated as one of the best 3-D sonic games by some fans.
And it starts with it's philosophy. Ask yourself this "Why do people buy sonic games?", is it for the incredible speeds or for playing as his roommates?. Welp the answer is simple, OF COURSE FOR PLAYING AS HIS ROOMMATES, because the character isn't based around speed, and had an entire marketing gimmick centered around that ( also about beign cool and edgy at the same time, but who cares ), we gotta make a game that forces you to play through one the worst stages until you can get to the only good one, and then go back to the horrible ones.
Appart from that the game's story is allright, but it is out of place in a sonic game for me, it wants to be edgy, yet the characters it has don't fit ( except for shadow, but that was his only trait, be the edgy guy, and becoming a joke in later years, and a lovable one ), it has it's high moments and lows, nothing really i can say about it, since i couldn't give more care to it and attention to it.
The gameplay falls back to the philosophy problem, but to summarize :
Sonic's ( or Shadow's) stages : OK, can get slow at sometimes, but when it decides to speed up, it's quite ok, not mentioning the homing attack;
Tails's ( or eggrobotnikman's ) stages : meh, it's the same as E-102 gamma, they have auto-aim but they tend to be slow, and the enemy placement is horrible;
Knuckles's ( or rouge's ) stages : "Why is this even here?", pretty self-explanatory, no one likes hide-and-seek with gems in random locations with a worse radar than the first Sonic Adventure, yet ironacly those were to only stages i got all "A" ranks because "game logic";
I could mention the music somewhat, but no need to repeat what other people already said, i like it.
A few more words before finishing is that there aren't as many sonic stages as his roommies get ( it's the same for everyone, maybe shadow got 3 at best ), and that really sucks the fun out of the game, because i buy a Sonic for speed and platforming, not for a shooter with auto-targeting and bad enemy placement, and most specially not for a treasure hunting game that keeps rewarding me for no reason. And i can't get behind why fans enjoy it, it has one the worst philosophies for a sonic game that i can think, and people say that you should just pick out Sonic's and Shadows's stages to enjoy the game, but the amount of them can be counted in just one hand ( not considering the last story ), and the game that was sold to me included those atrocities and they are hard to ignore.
Can't recomend it, if you are looking for speed and action, get something else, if you want something with Sonic, get Generations, already got that? my second best recommendation is Need for Speed Most Wanted ( the 2005 one, not the horrible Burnout : Most Wanted from 2012 ) since it has everything you could want, and some fun added with the cop chases.

